<title>USA: Boston 10-for-1 reverse split approved.</title>
<headline>Boston 10-for-1 reverse split approved.</headline>
<dateline>BOSTON 1997-06-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Boston Life Sciences Inc said on Monday that its shareholders approved a 10-for-1 reverse stock split.</p>
<p>The company said in a news release that the split takes effect Monday, and will reduce the number of common shares outstanding to about 12.5 million from approximately 125 million.</p>
<p>The company also said the conversion rate for preferred stock will similarly be adjusted on a 10-for-1 basis.</p>
<p>Boston Life said that as a result of the split, it will seek to move its listing from Nasdaq's SmallCap Market to its National Market.</p>
<p>Boston Life develops therapeutic products for cancer, autoimmune disease and central nervous system disorders.</p>
